This artifact ships as "plan-writing" and vendors the "writing-plans" skill from obra/superpowers.

Vendored file (upstream path):
  - skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md

References to un-vendored sibling skills (subagent-driven-development,
using-git-worktrees, finishing-a-development-branch) were softened to optional
notes so this artifact stands alone; the default plan-save path was changed
from `docs/superpowers/plans/` to the research-effort spec folder
`docs/specs/NN-slug/<stream>-plan.md` (co-located with its spec, tracked via meta.yaml).

The body is a Patronus behavioral adaptation aligned with the Codex, Pi and
OpenCode siblings: plans fix owned files, consumed/produced interfaces with
exact signatures, dependencies, test strategy and commands, and leave test and
implementation bodies to the implementer under tdd-cl. The upstream task
template with complete code in every step, its "No Placeholders" code mandate
and the zero-context-engineer framing were removed; the File Structure and
Bite-Sized Task Granularity sections (two to five minute steps) are retained.

